Z||000001||johnt671||09-09-2001||08:42 AM||||Not sure of the differecnes in years, but mine were out on my 84 so I found the screw on the back up switch by the shifter and adjusted it until they came on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LS1swap||09-09-2001||08:44 AM||||This happened on my 86 4 speed it was the switch under the stick. Have some stand behind the car and hold the sick all the way to the left and I bet they work. To get to the switch remove the ash trays and you will see 4 screws they are what hold the center shift counsel in place( shift  knob unscrews). Now this is for a stick never had an auto fiero but would guess it works something similar.opps just read your name you have an 87 that would be the  a five speed  rev, is to the right.<p>[This message has been edited by LS1swap (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||09-09-2001||04:09 PM||||Yes, must be the switch. I don't think it is under the console on the 5 speed's though. On my 86 w/5spd, the switch is on the tranny. And on my 86 SE w/4spd, it's under the console by the shifter.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LS1swap||09-09-2001||08:01 PM||||looks like there is a misprint in the 87 shop manual in the written description it says it is in the console but if you go to the ref. fig it shows it on the trans. i looked at my 87 5 speed and it matches the picture. it is the smaller of the two the big one is the VSS.<P>[This message has been edited by LS1swap (edited 09-09-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by LS1swap (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
